WEBVTT

00:08:29.176 --> 00:08:32.283
So I spent six years thinking about,
"How do you get out of this?

00:08:32.307 --> 00:08:35.467
What do you do with these moments
and how do you recommit your life

00:08:35.491 --> 00:08:36.842
to some sort of connection?"

00:08:36.866 --> 00:08:39.203
And my process is very much
the same process

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:41.279
that millions of people are going through.

00:08:41.303 --> 00:08:44.729
CA: So what do you see as
the key causes of that growing isolation?

00:08:44.753 --> 00:08:47.980
DB: I think it's a cultural thing,
a culture of hyperindividualism.

00:08:48.004 --> 00:08:51.570
In the 1950s, we had a culture
that was very communal.

00:08:51.594 --> 00:08:54.778
We had to face big challenges
like World War II and The Depression,

00:08:54.802 --> 00:08:58.153
and we had a culture that basically says,
"We're all in this together."

00:08:58.177 --> 00:09:00.381
And there were very rich
and tight communities.